comment -- `spawn`'s opposite, and it is deliberately *not* a container call. `Field` is
comment -- a fixed `[MAX_ROCKS]` SoA with a `live` count, so removing element `i` is the
comment -- swap-down the program writes by hand: copy the last live element over the
comment -- hole, then shorten. There is no `swap_remove` here because there is no `List`
comment -- here -- the two columns and the count are the whole data structure.
comment --
comment -- The shape is `swap_remove`'s and so is the consequence: this reorders, and an
comment -- index held across the call names a different rock afterwards (ch3 §11.13.7).
comment -- The difference is that a `List` names the cost in the method name, while an
comment -- SoA pool names it in the code the program wrote itself.
