comment -- The order-preserving cull, for a list something else indexes into. Survivors
comment -- pack forward and the tail is cut once (ADR-0050 §7).
comment --
comment -- **No `swap(i, j)` is needed and none exists** (ch3 §11.13.8): `Rock` is plain
comment -- data, so `rocks![w] = rocks[i]` is an ordinary copying assignment. A
comment -- container-valued element would move rather than copy (#15), which is why the
comment -- clause states the precondition instead of blessing the pattern generally.
comment --
comment -- `truncate(w)` is a **bound**, not an index, so `w == len` -- nothing culled --
comment -- is legal rather than the fault an out-of-range removal would be (ch3
comment -- §11.13.5, §11.13.3). This loop ascends, and correctly: it reads `i` and
comment -- writes `w`, with `w <= i` always, so nothing is written over before it is
comment -- read. `>..` is not a habit to acquire; it is the answer to `swap_remove`
comment -- specifically.
