comment -- The per-frame scratch list, and the dominant real use of `truncate` (ch3
comment -- §11.13.5). It is `persist` so the *buffer* outlives the frame while its
comment -- *contents* do not: `truncate(0)` at the top of every frame drops the elements
comment -- and keeps the allocation, so this list allocates once at cold start and never
comment -- again. A frame-arena list would allocate nothing but could not outlive the
comment -- frame; a fresh `List` each frame would allocate every frame. This is the
comment -- shape that does neither, and it is why `truncate` returns `()` and keeps the
comment -- buffer rather than handing back the dropped tail.
